From uafb003e064114795 at groups.google.com  Sat Dec 21 09:01:48 2024
From: uafb003e064114795 at groups.google.com (Finn Lindgren)
Date: Sat, 21 Dec 2024 09:01:48 +0000
Subject: Re: [r-inla] Re: Convergence issues: The Newton-Raphson optimizer did not converge
Message-ID: <LmjaA7Qg2UE.dKRiOA9uAgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <LmjaA7Qg2UE.Kpy8bedRAgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <LmjaA7Qg2UE.07I8sjY3AgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com> <LmjaA7Qg2UE.Kpy8bedRAgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/LmjaA7Qg2UE/m/dKRiOA9uAgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The spatial units, m or km, need to be chosen according to the size/scale of the modelling region. Metres can be fine for small regions. For larger scales, transforming to km is needed to avoid nunerical precision issues.

If all data have crs info, and a crs with km units is supplied to fm_mesh_2d, then the make.A functions etc can automatically map the data to the mesh.
If one want more control over that, use fm_transform() to convert the data to the km crs first.

crskm<- crs
fm_length_unit(crskm) <- "km"

Finn

